# Normalize text files to LF inside the repository. The working tree keeps the
# platform form, so core.autocrlf=true still checks these out as CRLF on Windows
# and nothing on disk changes.
#
# Why this file exists: git silently stops normalizing a file once its committed
# blob already contains CRLF. On 2026-07-24 a commit wrote CRLF into part of
# athena.py, scanner.py, market_structure.py and engine_b_quality.py, which
# disabled normalization for them — every later commit of those files then stored
# the whole pure-CRLF working copy and rendered the diff, blame and merge history
# unusable. Declaring the intent here makes it independent of any tool's settings.
* text=auto

# Windows shells are tolerant of LF, but these are launched by the OS rather than
# by git, so keep them explicitly CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
